user:
Compare these two estimates and extract structured analysis.

Primary Estimate: {primary_name}
Comparison Estimate: {comparison_name}

Category Deltas (largest differences):
{deltas_json}

Primary Line Items (sampled by category):
{primary_items_json}

Comparison Line Items (sampled by category):
{comparison_items_json}

Respond with JSON matching this structure:
{{
  "category_analyses": [
    {{
      "category": "category name",
      "primary_total": 12500.00,
      "comparison_total": 8200.00,
      "delta": 4300.00,
      "delta_drivers": ["3 window units at $450/each missing from comparison", "Labor rate difference: $65/hr vs $55/hr"],
      "line_item_evidence": ["Primary: Replace vinyl windows (3) $1,350", "Comparison: no matching item"]
    }}
  ],
  "scope_gaps": ["Comparison missing demolition allowance", "Primary includes permit fees not in comparison"],
  "overall_delta_direction": "primary_higher",
  "confidence": "high"
}}

Rules:
- delta_drivers: Explain WHY the numbers differ (missing items, quantity differences, rate differences)
- line_item_evidence: Quote specific line items that support the delta explanation
- scope_gaps: Note trades/allowances present in one estimate but missing from the other
- overall_delta_direction: "primary_higher", "comparison_higher", or "similar" (within 5%)
- confidence: "high" if clear evidence, "medium" if some inference, "low" if data is sparse
